# LF everywhere. A CRLF checkout on Windows breaks shell scripts the moment
# they are mounted into a Linux container, and the failure reads as "the
# container is broken" rather than "your checkout has \r line endings".
# `bash -n scripts/start.sh` is a CI step here, and against a CRLF copy it
# reports `syntax error near unexpected token` -- so without this the Windows
# leg of the matrix cannot be green.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.whl binary
